WEBVTT

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.160
KARAOKE

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:21.200
<i>The Hakone Mountains are the steepest</i>

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:24.080
<i>Even Hangu Pass can't compare</i>

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.750
<i>They're ancient and tall</i>
<i>With a bottomless...</i>

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:27.950
Let's stop.

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:31.330
Oh, don't stop!

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:35.290
Now that Retsuko is not around,
we have no choice but to sing.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:39.080
We don't have to sing.
I don't even know this song.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.080
But 'Hakone Mountains' is a classic!

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.080
Didn't you learn it at school?

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:47.160
Back in my day, we didn't need to.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.950
Let's go grab some food.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:58.870
You are right.

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:02.040
How about the place with the quiche?

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.500
You really like it there, don't you?

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:07.200
Well, it's so yummy!

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:16.160
REQUEST RECEIVED

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:17.330
RAGE

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:03.160
<i>I'm happy now.</i>

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:06.160
<i>The way he eats is messy...</i>

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.620
<i>but it's cute and childlike, so I'm happy.</i>

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:13.370
<i>Even the way he sniffs his fingernails</i>
<i>in public...</i>

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.700
<i>is quirky, so I'm happy!</i>

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:21.950
<i>Just walking together</i>
<i>with my nice boyfriend...</i>

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.910
<i>I feel truly blessed.</i>

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:37.500
Here!

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:42.120
And here! And here!
What do we have here?

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.830
It's all wrong!

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.040
Way too many mistakes!

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.750
How can I trust you to do it right?

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:51.790
I'm so sorry... I'll fix it.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.250
You've been acting strange lately.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:58.370
You used to be better at this.

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:01.200
Did something happen?

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:03.870
I'll fix it.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.700
TEA ROOM

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:25.410
-Hey, Fenneko.
-What?

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:29.370
Is Retsuko seeing someone?

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.290
What are you talking about?

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:37.410
Don't play dumb... It's obvious.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.830
You must know something, right?

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:45.450
I think...
It's probably Resasuke from Sales.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.870
I didn't see it coming.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:49.910
Sorry...

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:52.750
Why are you apologizing?

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:01.750
I want to punch him.

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:24.580
Look at this!
I've lost three kilos already!

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:28.870
I didn't even know.
It means that yoga is working.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.370
You're not losing weight.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:34.580
You're being worn out.

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:39.080
Here's what I think.

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:42.410
You're only pretending
to be a happy girlfriend.

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:46.160
It's the same thing at work -
pretending to be a good employee.

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:49.410
That's not the real you.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.450
Maybe it is.

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:56.950
There's nothing wrong with pretending.

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:58.700
Come on, Washimi!

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:01.790
Sometimes you have to act
in a relationship.

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:04.370
That's how you can make each other happy.

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:06.450
But...

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:09.290
only if you and your boyfriend

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:12.830
have the capacity to keep up the act.

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:14.660
Do you?

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.370
Welcome.

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:28.500
Please take your time and look around!

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:31.250
That's cute!

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:34.000
Do you like it?

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:39.160
-It's quite cute, isn't it?
-Yeah.

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:41.870
How about this one?

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:46.330
-Is this one cuter?
-Yeah.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:51.870
-I wonder if the first one is better.
-Yeah.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:55.700
Actually, both are pretty bland.

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:58.000
Yeah.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:02.120
Are we leaving?

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:04.040
Just going to the restroom.

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:06.200
OK.

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:14.290
<i>It hurts...</i>

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:22.290
RAGE

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:28.620
After I count to ten,
I'll be a happy girlfriend.

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:30.870
After I count to ten,
I'll be a happy girlfriend.

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:36.410
After I count to ten,
I'll be a happy girlfriend.

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:40.660
BAR

00:06:57.790 --> 00:06:59.620
Damn it!

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:12.200
I'm pathetic.

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:24.160
Damn! Why now, of all times?

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:28.750
Director Ton! What should we do?
You have golf tomorrow...

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:30.950
Idiot! Cancel it!

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:34.330
The end of the quarter
is fast approaching,

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:37.120
but we have staff shortages.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:38.790
Haida is out!

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:42.410
He has developed pneumonia
and has been admitted to hospital.

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:43.870
What a slacker!

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:45.330
Then there's Tsubone.

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:47.830
She tried to open one of her jars at home.

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:50.040
She fractured her wrist
and is out of action!

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:51.200
We should ban her jars.

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:55.910
And Kabae - she was accused of spying
and was detained by the authorities!

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:57.950
Who would have thought?

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:04.200
To make up for their absence,
knuckle down and work as a team.

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:07.290
Actually... We're four workers down.

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:18.200
You're no good to us in this state.
Make tea and keep out of the way!

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:30.370
Next!

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:36.750
Next! Next! Keep them coming!

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:39.080
That's some crazy speed.

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:43.040
We've got computers,
but he's still faster than us.

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:44.540
Hey, Fenneko!

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:48.620
Check these invoices again!
I can't approve them!

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:50.290
Yes!

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:57.370
-The analog generation sure is something!
-Go back to square one!

00:08:57.830 --> 00:09:00.160
I'll make some tea.

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:03.250
TEA ROOM

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:17.410
I want a cup of coffee.

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:19.580
Of course, I'll make you some.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.790
No, I'll make it myself.

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:34.500
I'm sorry that I can't help out
during this busy time.

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:44.330
No mistakes, down to the last yen.

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:49.500
Accurately counting the money
that comes in and goes out -

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:51.950
that's what accounting is.

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:56.000
Once someone messes up,
they keep doing it.

00:09:56.620 --> 00:10:01.290
The more mistakes they make, the more
the company and its people suffer.

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:05.830
How long will you keep messing up?

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:09.750
If you keep giving out more
than you get back in return,

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:12.000
there won't be anything left in the end.

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:13.790
Do you understand?

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:16.910
I think so...

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:20.120
He's not a bad person...

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:24.370
I wouldn't know.

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:31.410
I know you hate long lectures
from your shitty boss.

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:42.330
Please...

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:45.040
give me something to do!

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:49.450
Come on, then.

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:55.950
Companies exist to make possible
what we can't do on our own.

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:33.160
KARAOKE

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:37.000
Welcome... Party of three?

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:40.790
Party of two.

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:46.160
I come here all the time.

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:48.660
I didn't know you liked karaoke.

00:11:50.410 --> 00:11:51.250
I'm sorry.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:54.580
I've been lying to you.

00:11:56.450 --> 00:12:00.160
I haven't shown you the real Retsuko.

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:02.120
SEND

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:41.200
<i>Time for the truth about Retsuko!</i>

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:44.160
<i>Twenty-five years old, OK!</i>

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:47.290
<i>I'm a Scorpio, and my blood type is A!</i>

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:50.370
<i>I come to karaoke all the time</i>
<i>And bring my mic and then I...</i>

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:51.750
<i>Slay!</i>

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:56.370
<i>Heal the pain, in my secret place!</i>

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:59.540
<i>Underneath the smile</i>
<i>I'm metal till I die!</i>

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:02.660
<i>Underneath the smile</i>
<i>I'm metal till I die!</i>

00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:05.370
<i>Underneath the smile</i>
<i>I'm metal to the bottom of my soul</i>

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:11.500
<i>And that's a place that would destroy you</i>
<i>'Cause you're bland!</i>

00:13:18.410 --> 00:13:22.830
You're really good.
Don't mind me. Keep singing.

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:26.910
What should I put next?

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:32.000
<i>It's over.</i>

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:40.410
You really are an awkward girl.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.370
Welcome back, Retsuko.

00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:45.080
I'm back.

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:05.080
I'm home.

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:13.750
I told you not to bother coming here.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:16.790
-You look fine.
-I was worried over nothing.

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:20.330
It must have been tough in Accounting.

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:23.120
-It was hell.
-You owe us one.

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:27.330
I'll change the water.

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:31.450
See you. Take your time.

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:37.910
Retsuko, how are you doing?

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:41.700
What do you mean?
I should be asking you that.

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:44.410
I've heard some things...

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:47.080
about the guy from Sales.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:56.040
I think I know you better than he does.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:58.620
I've known you for five years.

00:14:58.950 --> 00:15:01.000
I'm sure I understand you.

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:07.580
But the truth is that
I probably don't know anything.

00:15:08.290 --> 00:15:12.540
The Retsuko that I know
is the one in my head.

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:17.250
That's why
I would like to know you better.

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:21.250
Do you catch my drift?

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:22.540
Yes, I do.

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:27.910
But if you don't ask properly,
I can't give you a proper answer.

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:31.540
I see... Of course...

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:37.000
You know what?

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:47.200
<i>Life doesn't always go the way you expect.</i>

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:53.290
<i>It's a series of disappointments</i>
<i>and misunderstandings...</i>

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:54.290
KARAOKE

00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:59.120
<i>...but we must work through our discontent</i>
<i>and move forward.</i>

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:06.450
<i>When we keep moving, we become</i>
<i>a little stronger every single day.</i>

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:24.790
Hey, short-timer! I told you to prepare
the documents for the meeting.

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:27.080
-Bring them here now.
-Coming!

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:29.830
-Open this jar, Retsuko.
-OK!

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:31.500
-Now feed me.
-Sure!

00:16:31.580 --> 00:16:34.750
-Retsuko, pick up the phone already!
-Alright!

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:37.950
This is only between us, OK?
I did this and that became...

00:16:38.040 --> 00:16:39.950
Retsuko, could you do this?

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:43.660
Your documents are ready.

00:16:45.410 --> 00:16:46.830
Excuse me!

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:52.540
What is this?

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:56.660
You think that's done?

00:16:57.250 --> 00:17:01.000
Always distracted!
You are the "pressure-free" generation.

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:05.500
I apologize. What should I fix?

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:08.580
Seriously, you don't even know...?

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:10.750
You, slow-witted woman.

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:13.500
It's common knowledge, isn't it?

00:17:15.330 --> 00:17:18.790
Listen, when you staple documents...

00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:25.500
you have to staple them
at a 45-degree angle!

00:17:58.540 --> 00:18:00.540
Subtitle translation: John Haguewood
